course: dictionary
lesson: 7812
title: Quick: fast, short, or clever?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «Be quick!» means hurry up, so quick means fast. «I'll have a quick shower» means a short shower, one that does not take long.
explain: A quick person understands or reacts fast. Think of a quick-witted hero in a story: he thinks fast and gets out of trouble. Quick can also mean done in a short time, like a quick look or a quick snack.
explain: «Quick, hide!» is informal and sounds urgent, so quick is used like an adverb here, meaning quickly. A good check is to swap in another word. If «quickly» fits and still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Quick means fast, or done in a short time.
fact: A quick person understands or reacts fast.
fact: «A quick check» means estimating to see if an answer makes sense.
fact: «The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog» is a pangram: a sentence that uses every letter of the alphabet at least once.
fact: Being too quick on the road can cause accidents, so crossing should be careful, not rushed.
exercise: «I'll have a quick shower before school.» What does quick mean here? | *Fast and short, not long | Full of soap | Loud and noisy | Cold and wet
exercise: «Lily sets her own timer, so the stop is calm and sleep comes quicker.» What does quicker mean? | *Sooner, in less time | Louder | Later | Sadder
exercise: «Cats have one life; they are agile (quick and good at balancing).» Find and copy the word that means good at balancing. | life | cats | falls | *agile
test: «He is a quick-witted hero who thinks fast in danger.» What does quick-witted mean? | Heavy and slow | Angry and loud | Late for everything | *Clever and quick to understand
test: What does quick mean in «a quick check of the answer»? | To write it in pen | To change the answer completely | To ask the teacher for help | *To estimate in a short time to see if it makes sense
exam: «The quickest road back is a full, honest apology with no "but".» What does quickest mean here? | *Fastest, the most direct way to make things right | Longest and hardest | Most unusual | Most expensive
